.el .ds Aq '
.TH qsh-audit 1  "audit 0.4.3" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-audit \- Read this machine\*(Aqs own audit log: the authorization decisions `qsh serve`, `qsh listen` and `qsh serve \-\-to` recorded, newest first, filtered on this machine (`docs/CLI.md` §6.22)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh audit\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR] [\fB\-\-principal\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-action\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-resource\fR] [\fB\-\-decision\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read this machine\*(Aqs own audit log: the authorization decisions `qsh serve`, `qsh listen` and `qsh serve \-\-to` recorded, newest first, filtered on this machine (`docs/CLI.md` §6.22).
.PP
Read\-only and local only: it never reaches a remote peer, writes no audit record, and there is no command that deletes or shortens the log. Run it on the host whose log you want.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<RFC3339|N[smhd]>\fR
Only records at or after this time: an RFC 3339 timestamp, or a span back from now written `N[smhd]` (`90m`, `24h`, `7d`)
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<RFC3339>\fR
Only records at or before this time (RFC 3339)
.TP
\fB\-\-principal\fR \fI<PRINCIPAL>\fR
Only records of this principal (`device:<name>`, `user:<name>`, `fp:sha256:<base64>`, or `\-` for a connection with none)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-\-action\fR \fI<ACTION>\fR
Only records of this action (`session.open`, `file.read`, or `connect` for a connection\-level record)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\fR \fI<RESOURCE>\fR
Only records of this resource identifier, exactly as stored
.TP
\fB\-\-decision\fR \fI<allow|deny>\fR
Only records with this decision
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<N>\fR
Most records to return, newest first: 1 to 1000, default 100
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.4.3
